                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Markov Assumption**: Classical N-gram language models approximate the full joint probability $P(w_1, w_2, \\dots, w_T)$ by assuming a word depends only on the preceding $N-1$ words:\n  \\[ P(w_t \\mid w_1, \\dots, w_{t-1}) \\approx P(w_t \\mid w_{t-N+1}, \\dots, w_{t-1}) = \\frac{\\text{Count}(w_{t-N+1}, \\dots, w_t)}{\\text{Count}(w_{t-N+1}, \\dots, w_{t-1})} \\]\n- **Neural Autoregressive Shift (Bengio 2003)**: Replaces sparse discrete lookup tables with continuous dense embedding projections $E \\in \\mathbb{R}^{|V| \\times d}$, eliminating the curse of dimensionality and sharing statistical strength across semantically similar tokens.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Mathematical Equations\n- **Perplexity Metric ($PP$)**: Measures how well a probability distribution predicts a sample. Lower perplexity indicates superior predictive calibration:\n  \\[ PP(W) = \\exp\\left( -\\frac{1}{T} \\sum_{t=1}^T \\ln P(w_t \\mid w_{<t}) \\right) = 2^{\\text{CrossEntropyLoss}} \\]\n- **Smoothing Invariants**: Without smoothing (e.g. Kneser-Ney or Laplace), any unseen $N$-gram sequence results in probability $P=0$, causing perplexity $PP(W) \\to \\infty$.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\nclass NeuralLanguageModel(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, vocab_size: int, embed_dim: int, context_size: int, hidden_dim: int):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.embeddings = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, embed_dim)\n        self.linear1 = nn.Linear(context_size * embed_dim, hidden_dim)\n        self.linear2 = nn.Linear(hidden_dim, vocab_size)\n\n    def forward(self, inputs: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        # inputs shape: (batch_size, context_size)\n        embeds = self.embeddings(inputs).view(inputs.size(0), -1)\n        hidden = F.relu(self.linear1(embeds))\n        logits = self.linear2(hidden)\n        return logits\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Zero-Probability Multiplication**: Multiplying raw probabilities $\\prod P(w_t)$ causes floating-point arithmetic underflow. In production, always perform computations in log-space: $\\sum \\ln P(w_t)$.\n- **Exponential State Explosion**: In classical $N$-grams, memory complexity scales as $O(|V|^N)$. A vocabulary of $50,000$ words makes a 5-gram table require $50,000^5$ entries.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Understand why modern decoder-only transformers (GPT-4, Llama 3) remain autoregressive causal models operating under the chain rule of probability.\n- Cross-entropy loss during pre-training directly minimizes the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence between true text distribution and model logits."
