                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Semantic Latent Space**: Maps variable-length textual inputs into fixed-dimensional vectors $\\mathbf{v} \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ (e.g. $d=1536$ or $d=3072$) where semantic similarity corresponds to geometric proximity.\n- **Bi-Encoder Architecture**: Sentence-Transformers pass queries and documents through independent transformer encoders, projecting them onto a shared unit hypersphere $\\|\\mathbf{v}\\|_2 = 1$.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Metric Formulations\n- **Cosine Distance vs Dot Product**: When vectors are L2-normalized ($\\|\\mathbf{u}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{v}\\| = 1$), dot product equals cosine similarity:\n  \\[ \\text{CosineSimilarity}(\\mathbf{u}, \\mathbf{v}) = \\frac{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}}{\\|\\mathbf{u}\\|_2 \\|\\mathbf{v}\\|_2} = \\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\]\n- **InfoNCE Contrastive Loss**:\n  \\[ \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{InfoNCE}} = -\\log \\frac{\\exp(\\text{sim}(q, d^+) / \\tau)}{\\exp(\\text{sim}(q, d^+) / \\tau) + \\sum_{i} \\exp(\\text{sim}(q, d_i^-) / \\tau)} \\]\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cosine_similarity(a: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    # L2 normalize and compute dot product\n    norm_a = np.linalg.norm(a)\n    norm_b = np.linalg.norm(b)\n    if norm_a == 0 or norm_b == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    return float(np.dot(a, b) / (norm_a * norm_b))\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **The \"Lost in the Middle\" Effect**: Embedding long documents (>512 tokens) into a single mean-pooled vector averages out granular details, losing keyword precision.\n- **Dimensionality vs Latency**: Higher dimensions ($3072$) increase recall by $2-3\\%$ on MTEB but double HNSW RAM consumption and distance calculation time.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Use Matryoshka Representation Learning (MRL) embeddings (e.g. `text-embedding-3-large`) to truncate vectors to $512$ dimensions with $<1\\%$ accuracy degradation."
