                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Reasoning Trajectory Invariant**: Transformers are autoregressive next-token predictors that allocate a constant amount of FLOPs per generated token. Forcing explicit reasoning tokens expands computational depth for complex multi-step deductions.\n- **Zero-Shot CoT (Kojima et al.)**: Appending `\"Let's think step by step:\"` activates multi-step decomposition in pre-trained weights without manual few-shot exemplars.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Self-Consistency (Wang et al.)\n- **Self-Consistency Majority Voting**:\n  \\[ \\hat{y} = \\arg\\max_{a} \\sum_{i=1}^M \\mathbb{I}\\left( \\text{extract}(r_i) = a \\right) \\quad \\text{where } r_i \\sim P_{\\text{LLM}}(\\cdot \\mid \\text{Prompt}, T > 0) \\]\n- Sampling $M=5-10$ diverse reasoning paths at temperature $T=0.7$ and taking the mode answer boosts math accuracy on GSM8K by $15-25\\%$.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```python\nSYSTEM_COT_PROMPT = \"\"\"\nYou are an expert systems engineer. For every problem:\n1. Deconstruct the requirements and define all input constraints.\n2. Outline intermediate mathematical derivations explicitly.\n3. Verify boundary conditions before emitting the final answer.\nFormat:\n[Reasoning Steps]\n- Step 1: ...\n- Step 2: ...\n[Final Answer]\n...\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Post-Hoc Rationalization**: An LLM might generate intermediate reasoning that appears logical but actually diverges from the causal activation state that chose the final token.\n- **Cascading Arithmetic Error**: A calculation mistake in step 1 invalidates all subsequent dependent reasoning steps.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Program-Aided Language models (PAL): Delegate math and state logic to an external deterministic Python execution sandbox instead of relying on token generation."
