                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Grounding Invariant**: RAG isolates knowledge ingestion from model parameters, injecting verified real-time enterprise documents into the LLM context window to eliminate factual hallucination.\n- **Two-Stage Retrieval Architecture**: High-recall candidate generation (Bi-Encoder + BM25) followed by high-precision cross-attention ranking (Cross-Encoder Reranker).\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Fusion Equations\n- **Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)**: Combines dense vector and BM25 lexical rank positions without needing score normalization:\n  \\[ \\text{RRF Score}(d) = \\sum_{m \\in \\{\\text{Dense}, \\text{BM25}\\}} \\frac{1}{k + \\text{Rank}_m(d)} \\quad (k \\approx 60) \\]\n- **HNSW Indexing**: Constructs multi-layer Voronoi geometric graphs enabling $O(\\log N)$ nearest-neighbor graph traversal with $>95\\%$ recall.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```python\ndef reciprocal_rank_fusion(dense_ranks: list, sparse_ranks: list, k: int = 60) -> list:\n    scores = {}\n    for rank, doc_id in enumerate(dense_ranks):\n        scores[doc_id] = scores.get(doc_id, 0.0) + 1.0 / (k + rank + 1)\n    for rank, doc_id in enumerate(sparse_ranks):\n        scores[doc_id] = scores.get(doc_id, 0.0) + 1.0 / (k + rank + 1)\n    return sorted(scores.items(), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Arbitrary Token Slicing**: Splitting documents strictly by character count cuts code blocks or tabular rows in half, destroying semantics. Always use recursive heading/paragraph chunkers with $10-15\\%$ overlap.\n- **Query-Document Mismatch**: User queries are short questions (`\"how to fix bug 404\"`) while documents are declarative statements. Use HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings) to bridge the latent gap.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Measure RAG reliability using the RAG Triad: **Context Relevance**, **Groundedness (Faithfulness)**, and **Answer Relevance**."
