                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Scaled Dot-Product Attention**: Allows each token position in a sequence to dynamically attend to every other position with dynamic weight allocation:\n  \\[ \\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\text{softmax}\\left( \\frac{QK^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} + M \\right) V \\]\n- **KV Cache Optimization**: In autoregressive decoding, past Key and Value vectors are cached in GPU VRAM, converting token generation from $O(T^2)$ redundant re-computation to $O(T)$ forward passes.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Memory Overhead\n- **KV Cache Memory Formula**: For batch size $B$, sequence length $L$, layers $N$, heads $H$, head dimension $D$ with 16-bit precision:\n  \\[ \\text{KV Cache Size (Bytes)} = 2 \\times 2 \\times B \\times L \\times N \\times H_{\\text{KV}} \\times D \\]\n- **Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE)**: Encodes relative positional information by rotating Query and Key vectors in 2D sub-planes: $R_{\\Theta, m}^d \\mathbf{x}_m$.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```python\nimport torch\nimport math\n\ndef scaled_dot_product_attention(Q, K, V, mask=None):\n    d_k = Q.size(-1)\n    scores = torch.matmul(Q, K.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(d_k)\n    if mask is not None:\n        scores = scores.masked_fill(mask == 0, -1e9)\n    attention_weights = torch.softmax(scores, dim=-1)\n    return torch.matmul(attention_weights, V), attention_weights\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **VRAM Out-Of-Memory (OOM) during Decoding**: The KV Cache grows linearly with context length $L$. For a 70B model with $32\\text{k}$ context, standard MHA KV cache consumes $>30\\text{GB}$ per single request.\n- **Mitigation**: Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) where multiple Query heads share a single Key-Value head pair (used in Llama 3).\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Understand PagedAttention (vLLM) which treats GPU memory like virtual memory pages, eliminating $60-80\\%$ of internal and external memory fragmentation."
