                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **B+ Tree Index Invariant**: All data records (or heap pointers) reside exclusively in leaf nodes linked horizontally as a doubly linked list, enabling both $O(\\log N)$ point lookups and high-speed contiguous range scans.\n- **ACID Transaction Isolation**:\n  - **Read Committed**: Prevents Dirty Reads using MVCC snapshot visibility.\n  - **Repeatable Read**: Prevents Non-Repeatable Reads via transaction-level read views.\n  - **Serializable**: Eliminates Phantom Reads and write skew using SSI (Serializable Snapshot Isolation).\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)\n- **WAL Invariant**: Log records describing data mutations must be flushed to non-volatile disk storage before dirty pages in the buffer pool are written to data files, guaranteeing crash durability ($D$).\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```sql\n-- High-performance composite index covering query filters & sorting\nCREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_org_created \nON users (organization_id, created_at DESC) \nINCLUDE (email, status);\n\n-- Explain analyze verifies index scan vs sequential scan\nEXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)\nSELECT email, status \nFROM users \nWHERE organization_id = 'org_491' \nORDER BY created_at DESC \nLIMIT 20;\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Leftmost Prefix Index Rule**: A composite index on `(A, B, C)` cannot accelerate queries filtering only on `B` or `C` without `A`.\n- **Index Column Function Wrapping**: Queries like `WHERE LOWER(email) = '...' ` ignore standard indexes on `email`. Use functional indexes `CREATE INDEX ON users (LOWER(email))`.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Understand Write Amplification and Table Bloat in PostgreSQL due to MVCC dead tuples, and tune `autovacuum` thresholds for write-heavy tables."
