                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Declarative Synchronization Invariant**: React effects synchronize state with external systems (DOM, WebSockets, APIs) *after* render and paint.\n- **Fiber Reconciler**: Breaks rendering work into interruptible units of work, diffing Virtual DOM trees using heuristic $O(N)$ reconciliation with unique keys.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Dependency Arrays\n- **Object.is Shallow Equality**: React compares dependency array elements using `Object.is(prev, next)`. Passing inline object/function literals triggers infinite render cycles.\n- **Cleanup Invariant**: Returned functions run before the next effect execution and on component unmount to tear down subscriptions and abort active HTTP requests.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```typescript\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\nexport function DataStreamComponent({ endpoint }: { endpoint: string }) {\n  const [data, setData] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n\n    async function fetchData() {\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(endpoint, { signal: controller.signal });\n        const json = await res.json();\n        setData(json.payload);\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        if (err.name !== 'AbortError') console.error(err);\n      }\n    }\n\n    fetchData();\n    // Cleanup prevents race conditions and memory leaks\n    return () => controller.abort();\n  }, [endpoint]);\n\n  return <div>{data || 'Loading stream...'}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Stale Closures**: An effect or callback capturing a state variable without listing it in its dependencies will read outdated values across renders.\n- **State Updates on Unmounted Components**: Failing to abort fetch requests or clear timeouts causes React state update warnings and memory leaks.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Use `useTransition` to keep the UI responsive during expensive updates, separating urgent interactions (typing in input) from non-urgent transitions (filtering a massive table)."
