                "notes": "### 📌 Architectural Overview & Core Invariants\n- **Reconciliation Loop Invariant**: Kubernetes controllers continuously compare Current State vs Desired State stored in `etcd` and execute operations to eliminate divergence.\n- **Pod Lifecycle & Probes**:\n  - **Startup Probe**: Disables liveness/readiness checks during slow JVM / model initialization.\n  - **Liveness Probe**: Detects process deadlocks; failing triggers `kubelet` container restart.\n  - **Readiness Probe**: Controls service endpoint routing; failing isolates the Pod from receiving ingress traffic.\n\n### ⚙️ Mechanics & Network Model\n- **ClusterIP vs NodePort vs LoadBalancer**:\n  - **ClusterIP**: Stable internal VIP with `iptables` or `IPVS` packet rewriting for intra-cluster traffic.\n  - **Pod-to-Pod Invariant**: Every Pod gets a unique routable IP without NAT across all cluster nodes.\n\n### 💻 Production Implementation Pattern\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: api-service\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: api\n        image: myrepo/api:v1.2.0\n        resources:\n          requests: { cpu: \"250m\", memory: \"512Mi\" }\n          limits: { cpu: \"1000m\", memory: \"1Gi\" }\n        readinessProbe:\n          httpGet: { path: /health/ready, port: 8080 }\n          periodSeconds: 5\n        livenessProbe:\n          httpGet: { path: /health/live, port: 8080 }\n          periodSeconds: 10\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Interview Traps & Failure Modes\n- **Identical Liveness and Readiness Endpoints**: If the database goes down and your liveness probe checks DB connectivity, all Pods in the cluster restart simultaneously in a catastrophic cascading failure loop.\n- **OOMKilled vs CPU Throttling**: Memory exceeding `limits` causes immediate kernel `OOMKilled` (SIGKILL 9). CPU exceeding `limits` triggers CFS throttling (latency spikes) without killing the process.\n\n### 🎯 FAANG Key Takeaways\n- Always specify CPU/Memory requests and limits, configure PodDisruptionBudgets (PDB), and leverage horizontal pod autoscaling (HPA) based on custom Prometheus metrics."
